<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?><rss xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" version="2.0"><channel><title>World News, Today World News, Latest International News, World Breaking News, Trending News of World - Times of India</title><link>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world</link><description>World News Today: Read the latest world news headlines, Current International breaking news world wide. In depth analysis and top news headlines world wide.</description><language>en-gb</language><lastBuildDate>2026-11-06T19:11:05+05:30</lastBuildDate><atom:link type="application/rss+xml" rel="self" href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/rssfeeds/296589292.cms"/><copyright>Copyright:(C) Fri, 06 Nov 2026 19:11:05 IST Bennett Coleman &amp; Co. Ltd, http://in.indiatimes.com/policyterms/1554651.cms</copyright><docs>http://syndication.indiatimes.com/</docs><image><title>World News, Today World News, Latest International News, World Breaking News, Trending News of World - Times of India</title><url>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/507610.cms</url><link>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world</link></image><item><title><![CDATA[North Carolina court revives roofing firm's lawsuits against insurers over unpaid storm repairs]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135609490.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[A North Carolina appeals court has reinstated lawsuits from Piedmont Roofing Services against various major insurance companies. Overturning an earlier trial judge's dismissal of breach of contract claims, the court concluded that sufficient grounds exist for the roofing company to pursue its claims. This ruling sheds light on the intricate legal issues related to the transfer of insurance rights in property damage situations.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-north-carolina-roofing-company-repaired-storm-damaged-homes-but-said-insurers-refused-to-pay-for-the-work-after-41-lawsuits-were-dismissed-a-november-appeals-ruling-revived-the-contract-claims-against-the-insurers/articleshow/135609490.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-north-carolina-roofing-company-repaired-storm-damaged-homes-but-said-insurers-refused-to-pay-for-the-work-after-41-lawsuits-were-dismissed-a-november-appeals-ruling-revived-the-contract-claims-against-the-insurers/articleshow/135609490.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-06T19:05:07+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135609668,imgsize-240004.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Trump had demanded that Harmeet K Dhillon be fired after he watched her on 60 Minutes on October 18: Report]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135609672.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/trump-had-demanded-that-harmeet-k-dhillon-be-fired-after-he-watched-her-on-60-minutes-on-october-18-report/articleshow/135609672.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/trump-had-demanded-that-harmeet-k-dhillon-be-fired-after-he-watched-her-on-60-minutes-on-october-18-report/articleshow/135609672.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-06T19:07:24+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Poulomi Ghosh</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135609732,imgsize-60568.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Eva Longoria-backed charity supports 100+ children at Vietnam orphanage, expands plans to Spain therapy centre]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135604673.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Since 2018, the Global Gift Foundation has championed the Quang Chau Orphanage, now known as Casa Ángeles, providing care to over 100 needy children. This initiative, bolstered by funds from the Global Gift Gala in Paris, also supports the Casa Ángeles therapy centre in Spain. Through engaging performances and a vibrant auction, the event helps sustain vital projects aimed at uplifting vulnerable communities.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-2018-a-charity-championed-by-eva-longoria-began-supporting-a-neglected-orphanage-in-vietnam-today-it-cares-for-over-100-children-and-a-november-5-paris-gala-aimed-to-fund-its-work-and-a-therapy-centre-in-spain/articleshow/135604673.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-2018-a-charity-championed-by-eva-longoria-began-supporting-a-neglected-orphanage-in-vietnam-today-it-cares-for-over-100-children-and-a-november-5-paris-gala-aimed-to-fund-its-work-and-a-therapy-centre-in-spain/articleshow/135604673.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-06T18:30:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135604870,imgsize-51392.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[At 9, she started feeding hungry children; now her nonprofit has reached over 110,000 people]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135606424.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[New Jersey teenager Anakh Sawhney started Rice Kids in 2018, aged nine, to provide meals to hungry children. Her nonprofit has since supported more than 110,000 people across five US states and parts of India through food, education, healthcare and other essential resources. More than half of the students supported by the organisation in India have returned to mainstream education.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/meet-anakh-sawhney-the-new-jersey-girl-who-began-feeding-hungry-children-at-9-eight-years-later-her-nonprofit-has-supported-over-110000-people-across-the-us-and-india-and-helped-students-return-to-school/articleshow/135606424.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/meet-anakh-sawhney-the-new-jersey-girl-who-began-feeding-hungry-children-at-9-eight-years-later-her-nonprofit-has-supported-over-110000-people-across-the-us-and-india-and-helped-students-return-to-school/articleshow/135606424.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-06T18:30:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135606821,imgsize-33476.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Michigan brother ploughs landscaped strip beside sibling's home, triggering bitter land dispute]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135597160.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[A Michigan appeals court revived a couple's claim over a 0.13-acre strip allegedly landscaped by their family for years. The dispute began after the husband's brother ploughed the land in 2022. The court ruled that a 1991 foreclosure judgment did not prevent the boundary claim, while leaving the $5,364.44 award for trespass and waste undisturbed.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-2022-two-michigan-brothers-became-embroiled-in-a-land-dispute-after-one-ploughed-a-landscaped-strip-beside-the-others-home-four-years-later-an-appeals-court-revived-the-boundary-claim-after-a-5364-award/articleshow/135597160.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-2022-two-michigan-brothers-became-embroiled-in-a-land-dispute-after-one-ploughed-a-landscaped-strip-beside-the-others-home-four-years-later-an-appeals-court-revived-the-boundary-claim-after-a-5364-award/articleshow/135597160.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-06T17:56:38+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135598259,imgsize-336474.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[New York buyer loses $1 million lawsuit after demanding $270,000 cut on $550,000 Bronx home deal]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135598186.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[A man from New York made a cash offer for a dilapidated home in the Bronx, agreeing to accept it in its current state. After finding additional issues just days before the closing, he sought a considerable price decrease. The seller declined, referring to the contract terms and previous property condition disclosures.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-new-york-buyer-offered-550000-cash-for-a-bronx-home-damaged-by-a-fallen-tree-then-demanded-a-270000-price-cut-and-sued-for-1-million-a-november-5-appeals-court-has-upheld-dismissal-of-his-lawsuit/articleshow/135598186.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-new-york-buyer-offered-550000-cash-for-a-bronx-home-damaged-by-a-fallen-tree-then-demanded-a-270000-price-cut-and-sued-for-1-million-a-november-5-appeals-court-has-upheld-dismissal-of-his-lawsuit/articleshow/135598186.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-06T17:55:41+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135598330,imgsize-68513.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Milo Ventimiglia says family is settled in new home after losing two houses in LA fires]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135598420.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Milo Ventimiglia and wife Jarah Mariano lost their home and another house under construction in the January 2025 Los Angeles fires, when she was 38 weeks pregnant. Nearly two years later, the actor says the family has settled into a new home with their two children, while reflecting on the loss, memories and rebuilding their lives.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-january-2025-milo-ventimiglia-lost-his-family-home-and-a-second-house-under-construction-to-the-los-angeles-fires-while-his-wife-was-38-weeks-pregnant-in-november-2026-he-said-they-had-found-a-new-home/articleshow/135598420.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-january-2025-milo-ventimiglia-lost-his-family-home-and-a-second-house-under-construction-to-the-los-angeles-fires-while-his-wife-was-38-weeks-pregnant-in-november-2026-he-said-they-had-found-a-new-home/articleshow/135598420.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-06T17:45:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135606315,imgsize-30038.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[US start-up plans to sell sunlight at night with India's Skyroot Aerospace]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135600533.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/space/american-start-up-plans-to-sell-sunlight-at-night-with-help-from-indias-skyroot-aerospace-a-scientific-study-warns-the-glow-could-affect-the-night-sky-up-to-30-kilometres-from-the-target/articleshow/135600533.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/space/american-start-up-plans-to-sell-sunlight-at-night-with-help-from-indias-skyroot-aerospace-a-scientific-study-warns-the-glow-could-affect-the-night-sky-up-to-30-kilometres-from-the-target/articleshow/135600533.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-06T17:55:19+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135600723,imgsize-990752.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Laura Loomer announces 'break' after GOP's midterm rout; but not from supporting Trump]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135606860.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/after-gops-midterm-rout-laura-loomer-announces-break-from-hosting-podcast-not-from-supporting-trump-or-offering-political-comments-cites-upcoming-wedding-as-the-reason/articleshow/135606860.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/after-gops-midterm-rout-laura-loomer-announces-break-from-hosting-podcast-not-from-supporting-trump-or-offering-political-comments-cites-upcoming-wedding-as-the-reason/articleshow/135606860.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-06T17:37:45+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Poulomi Ghosh</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135606907,imgsize-33248.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Republicans turn against Vivek Ramaswamy: 'He's a tech guy, Ohio is blue collar']]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135606252.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/republicans-turn-against-vivek-ramaswamy-as-ron-desantis-says-he-doesnt-know-why-party-backed-him-hes-a-tech-guy-ohio-is-blue-collar/articleshow/135606252.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/republicans-turn-against-vivek-ramaswamy-as-ron-desantis-says-he-doesnt-know-why-party-backed-him-hes-a-tech-guy-ohio-is-blue-collar/articleshow/135606252.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-06T17:18:43+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Poulomi Ghosh</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135606320,imgsize-60342.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Boy who started food bank with £40 at age 9 now helps 5,000 people annually across six sites]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135602352.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[After witnessing local families struggle with food insecurity, Isaac Winfield initiated a pop-up food bank in Redditch. This effort has grown into a well-established community service that supports thousands annually. The organization operates six sites and encourages donations without stigma or barriers. Isaac's mother highlights the positive community response and the inspiration his actions have sparked in others.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/meet-isaac-winfield-the-redditch-boy-who-began-a-food-bank-with-40-of-groceries-at-age-9-six-years-later-its-six-sites-support-about-5000-people-annually/articleshow/135602352.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/meet-isaac-winfield-the-redditch-boy-who-began-a-food-bank-with-40-of-groceries-at-age-9-six-years-later-its-six-sites-support-about-5000-people-annually/articleshow/135602352.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-06T17:06:12+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135602638,imgsize-144772.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Painting bought for $3,800 in 1963 hidden under fur coats for 40 years, now valued at $3 million]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135602150.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[In an astonishing find, a Georgia O’Keeffe painting that lay hidden for almost four decades in an East Village closet has come to light. Originally bought for $3,800 in 1963, it's now valued between $2 million and $3 million. With its auction set for November 18, a public exhibition will showcase the artwork at Rockefeller Center in early November.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-1963-a-new-york-family-paid-3800-for-a-georgia-okeeffe-painting-it-spent-nearly-40-years-hidden-under-fur-coats-before-resurfacing-with-a-2-million-to-3-million-auction-estimate/articleshow/135602150.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-1963-a-new-york-family-paid-3800-for-a-georgia-okeeffe-painting-it-spent-nearly-40-years-hidden-under-fur-coats-before-resurfacing-with-a-2-million-to-3-million-auction-estimate/articleshow/135602150.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-06T17:06:04+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135602234,imgsize-93003.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[ICE arrests foreign student at US airport while she heads for vacation with boyfriend]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135605744.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/ice-arrests-foreign-student-at-us-airport-while-she-heads-for-vacation-with-boyfriend/articleshow/135605744.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/ice-arrests-foreign-student-at-us-airport-while-she-heads-for-vacati