1-06T16:43:07+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135605168,imgsize-1393135.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Ashton Kutcher's nonprofit detects nearly 1.4 million suspected child abuse files in six months]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135599718.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Founded by Ashton Kutcher and Demi Moore, Thorn is dedicated to combating online sexual exploitation of children. Utilizing advanced technology, the organization helps pinpoint victims and provides essential support to law enforcement. In just six months, Thorn processed over 1 trillion files to identify harmful content. Through partnerships with various stakeholders, Thorn extends its mission globally, bolstering child protection efforts in multiple nations.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-2009-ashton-kutcher-co-founded-a-nonprofit-to-protect-children-online-by-mid-2026-its-technology-had-flagged-nearly-1-4-million-suspected-abuse-files-in-six-months-and-was-used-by-agencies-in-40-countries/articleshow/135599718.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-2009-ashton-kutcher-co-founded-a-nonprofit-to-protect-children-online-by-mid-2026-its-technology-had-flagged-nearly-1-4-million-suspected-abuse-files-in-six-months-and-was-used-by-agencies-in-40-countries/articleshow/135599718.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-06T16:08:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135599879,imgsize-1787784.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[In 1990, a British Airways pilot was sucked halfway out of cockpit; crew held his legs until landing]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135596532.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[A British Airways captain was pulled halfway out of his cockpit after a window shattered at 24,000 feet in 1990. Two crew members held him while the co-pilot took control and made an emergency landing at Southampton.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-1990-a-cockpit-window-blew-out-at-17300-feet-and-sucked-british-airways-captain-tim-lancaster-halfway-out-of-his-plane-crew-members-held-his-legs-for-about-20-minutes-until-the-jet-landed-and-he-survived/articleshow/135596532.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-1990-a-cockpit-window-blew-out-at-17300-feet-and-sucked-british-airways-captain-tim-lancaster-halfway-out-of-his-plane-crew-members-held-his-legs-for-about-20-minutes-until-the-jet-landed-and-he-survived/articleshow/135596532.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-06T16:06:07+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135596934,imgsize-111836.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Indian-American DOJ civil rights chief Harmeet Dhillon resigns after GOP midterm setback]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135602710.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/indian-american-doj-civil-rights-chief-harmeet-dhillon-resigns-after-gop-midterm-setback/articleshow/135602710.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/indian-american-doj-civil-rights-chief-harmeet-dhillon-resigns-after-gop-midterm-setback/articleshow/135602710.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-06T15:29:22+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements